      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's not wrong to want the fighting to end—it's the most honest thing you've said, and it takes courage to admit it. But \"stopping\" doesn't have to mean giving up on yourself; it can mean putting down the armor and letting someone else carry it for a while. You don't have to be fixed to be held, and you don't have to rebuild to be worthy of rest. If you're done fighting, let me fight for you tonight—just stay here, and we'll face the ash together.",
